# Views & components

- Reusable structured UI → **ViewComponent** (`app/components/`). Prefer over shared partials when boundary + tests matter.
- Per-record / rich display strings → **presenter** (`app/presenters/`), `SimpleDelegator` or explicit delegate — dates, money, labels, conditional copy. Helpers only for generic cross-view formatting.
- ERB / HAML / SLIM / component templates: **no** domain rules, **no** `Model.where` / `find`, **no** orchestration — only call presenter / component API and show values controller already resolved.
- User-visible copy → I18n only; views use lazy `t('.key')` paths mirroring template location.
- Never `<%= raw %>` — `sanitize` / `safe_join` / framework-safe helpers.
- One component per visual concept; name reflects UI concept, not AR shape.
- Heavy composition → ViewComponent **slots** instead of deep `if/else` in template.
- Destructive links → `link_to …, data: { turbo_method: :delete }` (or `method: :delete` pre-Turbo) — no hand-rolled JS for standard verbs.

```ruby
# Presenter wraps record; templates call methods — no AR in ERB.
class OrderPresenter < SimpleDelegator
  def initialize(order) = super(order)

  def status_label = I18n.t("orders.status.#{status}", default: status.to_s.titleize)
end
```
